A1. These always get sore when they are first put to work. ~ MUSCLES
A8. Something a hen lays on (one egg each day). ~ AVERAGE
A14. A gozinta. ~ ENTRANT
A15. It is worth its weight in gold. ~ CARAT
A16. What Europe seems to be bordering on now. ~ ASIA
A17. This gives you a key for any flat. ~ DO
A18. It will be yours some day. ~ TURN
A19. The end of a jag but the beginning of agony. ~ AG
A20. The Man on the Flying Trapeze! ~ SONG
A21. These belong to the victor. ~ SPOILS
A23. Found in the women's apparel section of a Tokio shoppe. ~ OBI
A24. Cash and carry. ~ LUG
A25. A pokerhouse stake. ~ POT
A26. Someone tried to make a goat out of this guy. ~ FAUN
A27. This will end your burdens. ~ ENS
A28. What an old actor has. ~ BEEN
A30. To get this out of a tub pull out the plug. ~ HORSE
A31. An abbreviated state. ~ SD
A32. What motorists do when they run out of gas. ~ SWEAR
A34. His full name. ~ SOUSE
A35. It, vim, S.A., pep, or what have you? ~ CHARACTER
A37. Rah material. ~ CHEER
A39. Cook will give you the recipe for these. ~ TOURS
A40. This starts the season out just right. ~ SE
A42. This is inclined to run down hill. ~ SLANT
A43. This is always blowing about something. ~ WIND
A44. This old bird used to raise elephants. ~ ROC
A45. An outgrowth that is now on hand. ~ WART
A46. "Somewhere a cow is bawling." ~ MOO
A47. Many crossword fans have been made from this bird's feathers. ~ EMU
A48. Cleopatra used this for a headache, the modern girl adds irin to it. ~ ASP
A49. This is always on the square. ~ CORNER
A52. All at sea. ~ ASEA
A53. Go to Halifax to get into this. (abbr.) ~ NS
A54. The only one who can sit on a policeman. ~ COOK
A55. Myself. ~ ME
A56. Not so bad. ~ GOOD
A57. This has become quite changeful since the depression. ~ PURSE
A58. A devilish place. ~ INFERNO
A60. What the family did for home comforts when on their vacation. ~ YEARNED
A61. When this gets hot it makes things crusty. ~ TOASTER

D1. A rash word. ~ MEASLES
D2. Off his nut. ~ UNSOUND
D3. Inoculations that make people smart. ~ STINGS
D4. Something rough and rocky. ~ CRAG
D5. Did you notice how Al has turned? ~ LA
D6. These are not found in the best circles. ~ ENDS
D7. There's no charge for this in a wire. ~ STOP
D8. A popular knee attribute. ~ ACTION
D9. To go over the line of defence. ~ VAULT
D10. Pulls a boner. ~ ERRS
D11. Scrammed. ~ RAN
D12. A goat without any go. ~ AT
D13. A speedy member of the MacHinery family. ~ ENGINE
D19. What an umpire gets for his services. ~ ABUSE
D22. A cut up on an organ. ~ OPERATION
D23. This dippy pair just love to get into a row. ~ OARS
D26. In some places they will only give you 3 of these for a dozen. ~ FOURS
D28. This is still bruin. ~ BEAR
D29. A side feature. ~ EAR
D30. He works up his own plot. ~ HOER
D32. This travels with a goat. ~ SCENT
D33. Do this before you start chiseling. ~ WHET
D34. Granddad's shirt button. ~ STUD
D36. Make a study of this. ~ CON
D37. What teachers are now facing. ~ CLASS
D38. There are many strings attached to this. ~ HARP
D40. The person who did it. ~ SOMEONE
D41. A door between Colombia and Peru. ~ ECUADOR
D42. Putting on the dog. ~ SWANKY
D43. The kind of puzzles that are not interesting. ~ WORKED
D44. A place owned by Amos Keeter. ~ RESORT
D46. A lodge member of the deer family. ~ MOOSE
D49. Hillbilly cider. ~ CORN
D50. To give vent to. ~ EMIT
D51. A dream separator. ~ RENO
D52. Things that women won't tell. ~ AGES
D54. K9. ~ CUR
